1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Guttorm bought his farm in 1828, and the year after he married back home in Hardanger. Guttorm and his wife were "haugianere" and were somewhat in opposition to the priest Hertzberg in Ullensvang. But the priest st
2 CONC ill mourned losing such strongly religious people. The couple was well known in Etne, and the farm was likely well managed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Guttorm seems to have been passed down from father to son for generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Etnesoga V page 52.
