1 NAME Sjur (Shur) Ingebrigtsson /Åse/
2 GIVN Sjur (Shur) Ingebrigtsson
2 SURN Åse
2 _MARNM Britson
2 NICK Saur
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 17 DEC 1822
2 PLAC Åse
2 ADDR
3 STAE Hordaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 JAN 1873
2 ADDR
3 CITY Roland
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Amerika : https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/110527660/shur-britson
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth No. 52, 17 Dec 1822: https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/11717/41
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/110527660/shur-britson
2 CONT
2 CONT Shur Britson BIRTH	15 May 1823 Rosendal, Kvinnherad kommune, Hordaland fylke, Norway '''(Wrong, birth 17 Dec 1822 Aase, Odda kommune, Hordaland fylke, Norway).''' DEATH	28 Jan 1873 (aged 49) Roland, Story County, Iowa, USA BURIAL	
2 CONC  Roland Cemetery Roland, Story County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Sjur (aka Shur) was the son of Ingebright Torkjellson and Ingejorg Jonsdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married his first wife, Engeborg Torkjelsdatter Ovrebo, in Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shur, Engeborg and their two-year-old daughter, Lena, immigrated to the United States in 1849 during the big year of emigration. They settled in Lisbon, Kendall County, Illinois.
2 CONT
2 CONT Engeborg died in Illinois during the cholera epidemic (March-August 1849).
2 CONT
2 CONT Shur and Engeborg had one daugher: 1) Isabelle Lena Britson (Mrs. John Danielson)(26 May 1846-30 Jul 1930).
2 CONT
2 CONT After Engeborg's death, he married Martha Hauge. Martha had a son from a previous marriage, Sjur Halvorsson "Sam" Hauge. Sam took the Britson name and was raised in the Britson household.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shur and Martha had the following children: 1) Sarah Britson (Mrs. Lars Christenson)(Oct 1853-) 2) Brit J. Britson (1855-1932) 3) John Britson (abt 1858-20 Aug 1880) 4) Martha Johanna Britson (Mrs. Hans A. Sexe)(abt 1864-15 May 19
2 CONC 36)
2 CONT
2 CONT It is important to note Shur's role as one of the early pioneers of Story county, in the Howard township area. There were three groups of Norwegian pioneers who left Illinois to make their homes in this part of the country, the fi
2 CONC rst in 1856, another in 1857 and the third the following year. From then on new settlers came steadily and the county was soon well inhabited. Shur, Martha, Lena, Sam and Brit, were among those traveling by wagon to establish the 
2 CONC first colony in 1856.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha Sjursdatter Hauge Britson 1819–1901
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Lena Britson Danielson 1847–1930
2 CONT
2 CONT Brit J. Britson 1855–1932
2 CONT
2 CONT John Britson 1858–1880
2 CONT
2 CONT Johanna Britson Sexe 1863–1936
2 CONT
2 CONT Gravesite Details There is another tombstone & memorial for him in Story City Cemetery, Story City, Story, Iowa.
