1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kvinnherad Gards- og ættesoga 5 page 182 Asalnes u. Sæbø øvre (26b).
2 CONT
2 CONT Bapt. Fjelberg pr.gj., Eide sokn 1859 No. E 125: https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/8273/76
2 CONT
2 CONT To America.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/136514886/malene_shaw
2 CONT
2 CONT Miss Thompson was born in Norway,Sept.28, 1859. She came to the United States when she was just 6 years old, with her parents where they settled in Ames, Iowa. She was married there to Abraham A. Shaw in 1883, and they moved to Mi
2 CONC nneapolis, Minn. where they made their home for 30 years.
2 CONT They moved to Opheim in 1912, in the Roanwood area, where they made their home until 1921. They farmed during this time and were active in the Lutheran Church, and community.
2 CONT She was a sister to Bertha Gamrath of this area. Mr Shaw died in 1921. From then on she made her home with her sister Mrs Carl Gamrath till 1937. She then made her home in Glasgow. She passed away in 1949.
