1 NOTE {geni:about_me} To America 1883.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/103681467/magrethe-valen
2 CONT
2 CONT Magrethe Rytvedt, daughter of Osmund Rygtvedt and Eli Natre, married (1) John Kallestadbakken ca. 1882. She married (2) Andrew O. Valen, son of Ole Valen and Anna Johnson, on 6 March 1901 in Story City, Story County, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magrethe (Margrete) was baptized in Skaanevik parish, Hordaland fylke, Norway. That was probably because her mother came from Indre (Inner) Matre in Skaanevik. Her parents were Osmund Gunnarson from Rugtveit (1827-1917) and Eli Vi
2 CONC ersdtr. from Indre Matre (1831-1887). Margrete grew up at Rugteit in Etne, Hordaland fylke. In 1882 she married Johannes Johannesson from Kaldestadbakken in Etne, born 1884. They stayed some month at his home before they emigrated
2 CONC  to America in 1883. A child was born in Etne: Inger Sissilie, b, 1882.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her death record listing her as Margaret Valen, names her parents as Osmund Rugtvedt and Ili Kallestadbakken.
